From c5d3e4e0c7d351236a50a10c0c202657c6368cf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 13:02:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(security): require real login for the dashboard and wire
 real user identity

Every route under (dashboard) -- parent, teacher, student, admin -- had no
session check at all and was reachable directly by URL with no login.
On top of that, every parent- and teacher-facing page independently
hardcoded "parent-1" / "teacher-1" regardless of who (if anyone) was
signed in, so every visitor saw and could act on the same single demo
family's billing, invoices, children, messages, and grading actions.

- Add src/app/[locale]/(dashboard)/layout.tsx: redirects to /login for
  any dashboard route when there is no session at all.
- Add src/lib/auth/currentUser.ts: requireParentProfile()/
  requireTeacherProfile()/requireAdminSession() resolve the *real*
  ParentProfile/TeacherProfile row for the logged-in user (via Prisma),
  redirecting appropriately when the role doesn't match.
- Replace hardcoded parentId/teacherId in all parent/* and teacher/*
  dashboard pages (billing, checkout, children, progress, reviews,
  notifications, messages, meetings, weekly reports, recommendations,
  enroll, payroll, assignments/grading) with the real logged-in
  person's id.
- Fix two remaining kidsarabicacademy.com contact emails on the privacy
  policy page (missed by the earlier robots.ts/sitemap.ts domain fix).

Note: the underlying data repositories (FinancialRepository,
CommunicationRepository, etc.) are still in-memory mocks seeded only
with the "parent-1"/"teacher-1" demo records -- a real logged-in user
will now correctly see an empty dashboard instead of someone else's
data, but persisting their real activity still requires migrating
those repositories to Prisma. Student-facing pages (14 files) have the
same hardcoded-id pattern and were intentionally left out of this pass;
flagging as a follow-up rather than leaving it unmentioned.

